## **How the Multi-Agent Workflow Works**

```
START
  ↓
🔎 RESEARCHER
  │ - Gathers information via local tools
  │ - Uses LLM to synthesize research notes
  ↓
✍️ WRITER
  │ - Reads research notes
  │ - Drafts content (3-5 paragraphs)
  ↓
🧐 REVIEWER
  │ - Critiques the draft
  │ - Either: APPROVED → proceed OR REVISE → loop back
  │
  ├─→ APPROVED? → ✅ COORDINATOR (finalize & save)
  │
  └─→ REVISE? → ✍️ WRITER (revise draft)
      │ (max 2 loops by default)
      ↓
      🧐 REVIEWER (review again)
      ↓
      [Loop or approve]
  ↓
✅ COORDINATOR
  │ - Finalizes output
  │ - Saves result via local tools
  ↓
END
```

**Key Points:**
- Pure Python orchestration (no external graph libraries)
- State passed between agents as dict
- Conditional routing (approve/revise loop)
- Budget-bounded revisions (max_revisions config)
- All agents use same local LLM

